# Design sequences - PUBLISHED as of 2026-11-03.
#
# These were withheld while each submission window was open. All four windows are
# now closed (EGFR, TNF-alpha, GLP-1R submitted; TfR1 closed 1 Nov unsubmitted), so
# the sequences are published with the write-ups that cite them.
#
# Kept for the record, because the withholding rule was twice written too narrowly:
# it first named each file individually, so a new round2_sequences.csv was not
# covered and got committed; then "submission/challenge2_*" named one challenge, so
# the first challenge 3 file was not covered either. Any future withholding rule
# must match by pattern, not by name.
#
# Challenge 5 (KRAS G12D pMHC) is open until 8 Nov. Its sequences go here, ignored,
# until that window closes.
#
# Caught a third time on 7 Nov, and only because the rule above was read before the
# files existed: the scaffold pipeline writes designed sequences into JSON result
# files, which "submission/challenge5_*" does not cover. Matching by pattern was not
# enough on its own - the patterns also have to cover every PLACE sequences are
# written, not just the submission folder.
# FOURTH time, 7 Nov: I enumerated mpnn_all/mpnn_candidates/specificity by name and
# then added run_mpnn_divergent.py, whose mpnn_divergent.json was not on the list. The
# commit was stopped by a guardrail, not by me. Enumerating names has now failed four
# times, so the rule is inverted: withhold EVERY json in pmhc/results by default and
# name the exceptions. A new output file is then withheld automatically, and the
# mistake is impossible to repeat in the same way.
# FIFTH guard, 7 Nov: the json rule was inverted but the csv rule was still
# name-based (*sequences*), which would not cover boltzgen_designs.csv. Inverted
# too: every csv and fasta in pmhc/results is withheld by default.
#
# WINDOW CLOSED 9 Nov 2026 11:59 UTC. Challenge 5 was submitted (20 designs, novelty
# check passed) and the submission window is shut, so the condition every rule above
# was waiting on has been met. The four withholding patterns below are therefore
# retired, exactly as challenges 1-4 were retired on 3 Nov, and the sequences are
# published with the write-ups that cite them. The comments above are kept because
# the five mistakes they record are the reason the rule was eventually written by
# pattern and by inversion rather than by name.
#
#   pmhc/results/*.json
#   pmhc/results/*.csv
#   pmhc/results/*.fasta
#   submission/challenge5_*

